      "id": "shell-snapshot-fix",
      "agent": "codex",
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "tier": "cheap",
      "prompt": "tools/swarm.mjs (Phase 1 lanes integration, already on HEAD) broke tests/field-lessons-batch-ag-runtime.test.mjs 'AG default relocates Codex and shell worktrees without a config key' (expected 1 input.txt under the root, got 2). Cause: for claude shell jobs, `prepare` in runManifestBody writes a verified copy of every context/output file to `.swarm/runs/<id>/snapshots/<job>/<attempt>/` inside the project root, and executeClaudeShellJob copies from that `snapshotRoot`. Lesson AG forbids copies of project files under the root when worktrees are relocated. Fix: remove the on-disk snapshot directory. Have `prepare` return the verified bytes and modes for that job's files in memory (only for claude shell jobs, only for the in-flight job), and have executeClaudeShellJob write those bytes into its worktree instead of re-reading `snapshotRoot`/root (a file verified absent is removed, as today). Keep the snapshot-changed check exactly as is. Minimal change; touch nothing else. Run `node --import ./tests/_isolate-config.mjs --test tests/field-lessons-batch-ag-runtime.test.mjs tests/lanes-run.test.mjs tests/claude-shell.test.mjs tests/swarm.test.mjs` (some shell tests need a real sandbox-exec and may be skipped/failing inside your own sandbox; say which).",
